   {
    "id": "q5",
    "text": "Does a tick on the same clock as a packet or frame event order before it?",
    "default": "The tick is counted first, so the uptime includes it",
    "reason": "Request says the uptime includes the tick that made the frame due",
    "answer": "The tick is counted first, so the uptime includes it",
    "status": "defaulted",
    "by": "oracle",
    "evidence": null
   },
   {
    "id": "q6",
    "text": "Is the telemetry period in register 6 changed by a start with period 1 to 3, and what does a start with a period of 0 do when the period is still 100?",
    "default": "Period 1 to 3 gives 4; zero keeps the current period",
    "reason": "Request wording",
    "answer": "Partly. The spec does not put the telemetry period in register 6: offset 6 is TIDX, the held-frame word index (RW, bits [6:0]). The period is set by a TLM_START command, which the spec does not map to a register offset. Within that pacer rule, a start with period 1 to 3 sets the period to 4, and a start with period 0 keeps the current period (100 after reset). Your proposed default matches the spec.",
    "status": "answered",
    "by": "oracle",
    "evidence": "Pacer: TLM_START restarts the count (period 0 keeps, below 4 raised to 4); a frame falls due every period ticks; one held frame; overruns dropped; STOP forgets the held frame; TAKE releases it."
   },
