    "id": "q7",
    "text": "Does a telemetry start restart the tick count to the next due tick, and is the held frame kept?",
    "default": "The due counter restarts at zero; a held frame is kept",
    "reason": "Request says restarts the count and only stop forgets a frame",
    "answer": "Partly specified. TLM_START restarts the count, and the held frame is kept, because only STOP forgets a held frame. The spec does not say the count restarts at zero or what the next due tick is, so the proposed default's 'restarts at zero' is not confirmed.",
    "status": "answered",
    "by": "oracle",
    "evidence": "Pacer: TLM_START restarts the count (period 0 keeps, below 4 raised to 4); a frame falls due every period ticks; one held frame; overruns dropped; STOP forgets the held frame; TAKE releases it."
   },
